[Assault.FullName]
Whirlwind
[Assault.Description]
The initial phases of Operation Overlord have been a success but now its time to strike deeper into enemy occupied Normandy. Progress inland is coming at a steep price though as the Germans are entrenching every village and strategic location that they can. Topography is also working against the allies as the unique terrain in this sector is limiting maneuverability.

[Tanks_Battle.FullName]
Steel Torrent
[Tanks_Battle.Description]
The German army has again found itself encircled. The Fuhrer himself has issued the order that this encirclement must be breached. Battlefield command is preparing to force a breakout with a decisive armor thrust. Once a hole is punched into the enemy lines, our forces will be able to create great havoc in the enemy lines and rejoin with our remaining forces in the area.

[Battle_Heroes.FullName]
Acts of Bravery
[Battle_Heroes.Description]
Operation Typhoon, the drive on Moscow began on October 2nd, 1941. By December, German advance units were a mere 15 miles away from the Kremlin, but they were unprepared for the violent winter blizzards that befell them. As the German advance began to flounder and stall, Zhukov was able to mass nearly a half a million men in the Moscow operational sector and launched a counter-attack on December 5th.

[Paratroopers.FullName]
The Razor’s Edge
[Paratroopers.Description]
The main advantage of Airborne troops is their ability to strike behind enemy lines and capture and defend key bridges and road junctions until heavier friendly units can arrive.  They were used to great effect both in the hours before D-Day and during Operation Market Garden.

[Mortain.FullName]
Mortain Counterattack
[Mortain.Description]
Thanks to the success of Operation Cobra, General Omar Bradley started to make rapid progress at the beginning of August. By August 4th, The German units facing off against Bradley had largely collapsed. A small but fierce German counter-offensive codenamed Operation Luttich was launched late of the evening of August 6th at Mortain. This was a last-ditch attempt at halting the Allied breakthrough but it was halted within a week.

[Vojsko_Polskoe.FullName]
Command Decisions
[Vojsko_Polskoe.Description]
German troops crossed into Poland early on September 1. The Polish units stationed close to the border were quickly overrun and scattered. Polish Command and Control on the front is almost non-existent and for the time being, the only concerted defensive efforts are coming from independent unit commanders with no guidance from their superiors. 

[Last_Chance.FullName]
Last Chance
[Last_Chance.Description]
For various reasons, the German forces have delayed their final offensive against the fleeing Allied troops at Dunkirk. This brief respite has given the French army a chance to prepare their positions for the final German push into Western France.

[Commandos.FullName]
Behind Enemy Lines
[Commandos.Description]
The Soviet army is approaching the borders of the Third Reich itself. Both sides have been preparing for an eventual battle around the small town of Sandomierz. Special saboteur squads have been sent by the Soviet High Command to infiltrate behind enemy lines. They are tasked with scouting enemy positions and to destroy logistical assets and air defenses. Your squad must sabotage the POL and armament depot, spot and destroy any AA gun positions encountered, then return back to our lines alive (hopefully).

This task is not for the faint of heart, as you only have one elite special forces squad at your command. Utilize stealth and any enemy weapons you can salvage to accomplish your mission.

[firstday.FullName]
First day
[firstday.Description]
Operaton "Zitadelle" started in early morning of 5 July. 2nd SS panzer corps advanced at the south face of Kursk salient and encountered 52nd Guards and 375th Infantry divisions during the first day. Backed up with powerful artillery and aviation support, SS divisions gradually broke through. "Das Reich" kampfgruppe pierced the defence of 52nd Guards division by 15:00 and soviet command ordered 230th tank regiment to counterattack. Soviet tankers couldn't stop the SS advance and first defensive position of the army was broken by the end of the day.

[Nakanune_pereloma.FullName]
Turning the tide
[Nakanune_pereloma.Description]
4 July 1943 german forces started operation "Zitadelle". It's purpose was to encircle and destroy soviet forces in Kursk salient. Two simultaneous blows were delivered: in the north (Army Group "Center", Model) and in the south face of the salient (Army Group "South", Manstein). Manstein commanded best german units such as elite panzergrenadier division "Grossdeutschland" and SS panzergrenadier divisions "LSAH", "Totenkopf" and "Das Reich". It was planned to quickly pierce soviet defences near Oboyan and then move towards Kursk completing the encirclement.
It was clear by 9 July that this plan failed. German forces, despite initial tactical successes,  were unable to break-out and were bogged down by strong defence of 1st tank army (Katukov) and 6 Guards army (Chistyakov). Manstein and Hoth (commander of 4 panzer army) decided to shift the direction of offensive to Prokhorovka and ordered 2nd SS panzer corps (under the command of Paul Hausser) to do that.
10 July german units attacked 69th army positions (Kruchenkin), which was reinforced by two tank corps, and broken through. But units of 5th Guards army (Zhadov) and 5th Guards tank army (Rotmistrov), which were assigned to Voronezh front (Vatutin) from Stepnoy front, were already in a process of deploying near Prokhorovka. These forces were ordered to make counter-stroke against approaching SS units 12th July, but it was neccessary to stop german advance first and don't allow fascists to broke through to Prokhorovka rail station. 11th July was the day of hardest defensive fighting for soviet troops near Prokhorovka...

[Balaton.FullName]
Trap
[Balaton.Description]
26 December 1944 2nd and 3rd Ukrainian fronts finished encirclement of Budapesht.
German command started to prepare operation to relieve troops encircled in the city. 2 January 4th SS Panzer Corps with units of 6th Army begun offensive against 3rd Ukrainian front. There was a fierce fighting and offensive was stopped only in the end of the month.
In the morning of 7th January germans tried to break to Budapesht through positions of 20th Guards infantry corps. 2 panzer divisions, 503rd and 509th heavy panzer battalions, 2nd hungarian tank division along with separate tank ans SPG battalions were concentrated for this task.
Despite 20th infantry corps had enough artillery (including AT guns), soviet command reinforced it with 2 artillery regiments, 7th mechanized corps and 1st Guards mechanized corps.
Thanks to competent usage of artillery and tanks, german offensive was stopped by the end of the day.

[razvedkaboem.FullName]
Recon by force
[razvedkaboem.Description]
In early April 1945 Soviet forces prepared to assault Berlin from river Oder bridgeheads. Zhukov ordered all armies to begin reconnaissance in force operations on 11th April.
32 recon units, composed of infantry battalions, penal companies and engineer squads supported by SU-76 and ISU-152 batteries, were formed in area of 1st Belorussian front. These units were supported by artillery and mortar regiments. Recon units succesfully battled against the enemy for 2 days, captured first line of German trenches and held them. German defensive lines, weapon emplacements and artillery positions were reconnoitered.

[Childuve.FullName]
Battle in Szydlowe outskirts
[Childuve.Description]
August 1944, 03:00. Vanguard unit of 95th Guards infantry division, which was ordered to defend Khmelnik-Szydlow highway in Skadla-Rachitse area, was attacked by large group of enemy tanks and mechanized infantry. Vanguard was forced back to south-east with heavy casualties reported. Enemy forces continue their assault towards Szydlow town. You received the following order: "Relocate 1076th IPTAP to threatened area and stop enemy tanks" (IPTAP is special AT artillery regiment).

[OboronaRogani.FullName]
Defence of Rogan
[OboronaRogani.Description]
Red Army operation "Zvezda" ("Star") with the purpose of capturing Charkov and Belgorod began on 2nd February. II SS Panzer Corps («Liebstandarte SS Adolf Hitler», «Das Reich» and «Totenkopf») was the main German force in the area.
11th February. Units of 15th tank corps attacked 1st company of 1st panzergrenadier regiment of LSAH division, supported by several SPGs and 20mm AA guns, for entire day.

[lisow.FullName]
Trap for a Tiger
[lisow.Description]
501st heavy tank battalion performed not very well during late 1944 and it's commander major von Legat was replaced by major Samish. In addition, battalion became 424th (because number 501 was given to new SS heavy tank battalion). Battalion was attached to XXIV tank corps in December 1944.
On 15th January 1945 it assaulted Lisow village in Poland, which was defended by 61st Guards tank brigade and units of 10th Guards Ural voluntary corps with several tanks from 72nd Guards separate heavy tank regiment. After fierce fighting 424th battalion was completely destroyed. Major Samish and commander of 61st brigade colonel Morozov died in battle.




[Italians.Description]
\t The English have established a supply base in a settlement by the railroad station 20 km away from the frontline. This base is a key point in their defense system and is well protected from air attacks. Therefore Rommel decided to dispatch an Italian mountain rifle unit under his command to capture it.
\t Since the approach march to the base is planned to be conducted trough almost impassable mountain trails, standard heavy weapons will be unavailable. First, a small group of elite soldiers is supposed to take down the crews of enemy machine guns and field guns guarding the base; afterwards the whole unit is to attack, receiving air support. After capturing the base guns it will be possible to organize the defenses to last until the main German forces arrive that will attempt to breach the front and reach the base. Rommel reckons that it will draw the major part of the British reserves and the Italians will be able to stand up and hold their ground until his forces arrive.

[Italians.FullName]
A Bold Raid

[Sherman12345.Description]
\t The Americans managed to stop Rommel’s advance and counterattacked. Our forces are completely exhausted and have to fall back in the face of the unskilled, but overwhelming enemy. Major Gerhard and his PzKpfW VI Ausf H Tiger tank unit are assigned to cover the evacuation of the headquarters.
\t The reconnaissance group reports that considerable American forces are about to reach the location of the headquarters, even though the tanks and SPGs had to leave their infantry and artillery support behind. Despite the enemy’s advantage in numbers, high command is convinced that the qualitative superiority of the Tigers and their crews will ensure a successful completion of the mission.

[Sherman12345.FullName]
Qualitative superiority

[AlloutAssault.Description]
\t After Rommel’s advance petered out, the British command decided to attack the enemy, reorganizing surviving units and reinforcing its main attack force. One of the most important objectives was to capture an insular village, acting as a road network node in a favorable strategic location. Realizing this, the enemy turned it into a well fortified strong point with tank groups, AA and field artillery. 
\t You have been appointed commander of the British forces, assigned to breach the German defenses and capture the village. Considering the special importance of your mission, your orders will be issued by General Montgomery himself. All hopes of the United Kingdom are in your hands now, Sir!

[AlloutAssault.FullName]
All-out Assault
